      "name": "Gale Crater",
      "lat": -5.4,
      "lon": 137.4,
      "category": "Measured environment — Curiosity / REMS / RAD",
      "color": "green",
      "details": "Curiosity landing region. Radiation: early-mission absorbed dose about 210 ± 40 µGy/day (first ~300 sols, Aug 2012–Jun 2013); observed values about 180–225 µGy/day. Dose-equivalent estimate (~640–650 µSv/day) is a different quantity. Indicative pressure: 700–900 Pa. Elevation: about −4,400 m. Dust-storm visibility estimates depend on the analysis; do not equate opacity directly with visibility."
    },
