      "color": "green",
      "details": "Viking 2 landing region. Elevation: about −3,000 m. The supplied comparison file does not provide other comparable numeric measurements for this location."
    },
    {
      "name": "Jezero Crater",
      "lat": 18.4446,
      "lon": 77.4509,
      "category": "Measured environment — Perseverance / MEDA / SHERLOC / PIXL",
      "color": "green",
      "details": "Perseverance landing region. An ancient impact crater approximately 45 km wide, containing evidence of an ancient lake and river delta. Investigations include rock and regolith chemistry, mineral composition, geological layering, atmospheric pressure, temperature, wind, humidity and dust. Perseverance also collects rock and regolith samples for possible return to Earth."
    },
    {
      "name": "Gusev Crater",
      "lat": -14.5692,
      "lon": 175.4729,
      "category": "Measured environment — Spirit / APXS / Mössbauer / Pancam",
      "color": "green",
      "details": "Spirit rover landing region. Spirit investigated volcanic rocks, plains, soil and the Columbia Hills. Measurements included elemental composition, mineralogy, rock textures, soil properties and surface imaging. Some rocks and soils showed evidence of past interaction with water, including alteration by water-rich or hydrothermal processes."
    },
